WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.720
Tim Ferriss: We have questions that&nbsp;
were pre-submitted and then we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.320
questions that are coming in on the&nbsp;
live feed and I'll do my best to answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:29.960
a whole bunch of both. So why don't we dive in.
The first question I'll answer is from the live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:35.000
feed. This is from Zahir. "Are you actively taking&nbsp;
any actions to reduce your carbon footprint?"&nbsp;

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.720
Yes, I am. There are certainly a number&nbsp;
of different steps you can take in terms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:46.600
of funding new technologies. A lot of my&nbsp;
investing over the last, I would say three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:53.240
to four years has been in various types of tech,&nbsp;
different products and services that I think will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.240 --> 00:01:04.200
overall help people to reduce carbon footprint.
I also donate money monthly to different causes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:11.320
and companies including Charm Industrial,&nbsp;
which puts oil back underground. People&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:19.440
can check that out at charmindustrial.com.&nbsp;
And that, I believe, is now funded through,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:27.040
as it stands for me, Terraset. I believe that is&nbsp;
how I'm going about doing this, Terraset Climate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:33.800
so people can look at that as a means, for&nbsp;
instance, to hopefully offset some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:39.960
carbon footprint of my travel and other things.
I am intensely aware of individual action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:48.880
but also the necessity in a sense to, number one,&nbsp;
not try to consume our way out of this problem,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:54.000
but also simultaneously to recognize&nbsp;
that we do need better technology. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:59.240
it's a combination of different things.
All right, this is a question from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:05.840
live feed. "What classical career are you&nbsp;
