00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:32.760
set of universes or in the multiverse on other&nbsp;
tracks that are running parallel to this one.&nbsp;

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:38.960
Let me go to the questions that were&nbsp;
pre-submitted and I'll answer a number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:47.160
of those and we'll bounce back and forth. So the&nbsp;
next question is going to be from Lucas. "Hey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:50.760
Tim, you mentioned in an interview that you&nbsp;
allowed yourself to live your life unoptimized.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:56.120
Are you still living an unoptimized life?"
I would say that there's optimizing and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:59.520
deoptimizing happening simultaneously&nbsp;
in the sense that there are certain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:08.000
things that I am optimizing. To define&nbsp;
that simply tweaking variables to, say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:17.800
improve certain outputs based on the inputs.&nbsp;
Right? So looking for an elegant refinement in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:22.440
so much as I might approach something like&nbsp;
Occam's Protocol in The 4-Hour Body, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

