whatsoever. And I have used Dr. Bronner's&nbsp;
unscented Castile soap, so large containers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:50.760
of Dr. Bronner's unscented soap for pretty much&nbsp;
everything for years now. I refill my hand soap&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:56.800
with Dr. Bronner's and there are these devices&nbsp;
you can get on Amazon with mason jars that help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:56.800 --> 00:22:01.600
you to basically create foams doing this. So&nbsp;
you can put that in your bathroom or anywhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:09.880
else. And that is effectively all I use for&nbsp;
both my face, my head, and my body. And my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:09.880 --> 00:22:19.120
general approach with self-care is the fewer&nbsp;
chemicals, the fewer ingredients, the better.&nbsp;

00:22:19.120 --> 00:22:26.160
This has been my policy for a long time. It's also&nbsp;
why I tend not to use sunscreens. Occasionally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:26.160 --> 00:22:31.000
I'll use something that is predominantly, say,&nbsp;
zinc oxide if I'm going to be in a very harsh&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:36.240
set of conditions, for instance, especially if I'm&nbsp;
on snow or anything that's going to be reflective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:40.520
where I might get incredibly burned, then I&nbsp;
might use something like that. But otherwise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:40.520 --> 00:22:48.280
I will use long sleeve shirts, hats, et cetera&nbsp;
to minimize my sun exposure or take breaks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:52.280
right? I'll be exposed for 20 to 30 minutes&nbsp;
and then I'll take a break and I'll slowly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:52.280 --> 00:22:58.880
acclimate over time as opposed to putting&nbsp;
sunscreen with 30 ingredients on my skin.&nbsp;

00:22:58.880 --> 00:23:06.000
We've seen recall after recall after recall,&nbsp;
for instance, of sunscreens based on different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:13.520
carcinogens and so on. I'm not sure that's&nbsp;
helpful, but I will say that there is such a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:13.520 --> 00:23:23.000
thing as over applying chemistry and enhancements&nbsp;
to your body and your face. So I really try&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:31.320
to use a light hand and the less, the better.
I would also say that your external condition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:37.880
I think is often a reflection of your&nbsp;
internal condition. I do consume a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:49.400
of healthy fats. I take Nordic Naturals omega-3&nbsp;
supplements. I alternate between fish and algae,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:55.880
which has completely eliminated any type of&nbsp;
nausea that I have felt from other omega-3&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:55.880 --> 00:24:02.080
supplementation. As an example, I pay a lot of&nbsp;
attention to diet, so I would say I'm working from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:09.040
the inside out as opposed to trying to address the&nbsp;
cracks in the veneer with topical treatments. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:09.040 --> 00:24:14.440
I get this question a lot, so I wanted to take&nbsp;
a stab at answering it. I also think that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:14.440 --> 00:24:21.400
lighting and the camera are very flattering at the&nbsp;
moment. I do have crow's feet, large crow's feet.&nbsp;

