00:28:56.720 --> 00:29:01.000
what do you pay attention to? Do you have&nbsp;
FOMO about doing certain things and not other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:06.760
things? How do you incorporate all the advice?
And frankly, there are times when I experiment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:06.760 --> 00:29:13.040
with new types of advice and then there&nbsp;
are times when I hit pause and I say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:13.040 --> 00:29:18.520
"If I were to assume I know what to do, what&nbsp;
are the things I know I should do? What are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:18.520 --> 00:29:26.920
the things I know work?" Cold exposure,&nbsp;
resistance training, very basic meditation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:26.920 --> 00:29:34.000
20 minutes twice a day. There are certain&nbsp;
ingredients that are easy to neglect because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:39.920
they don't have the newness. They aren't the shiny&nbsp;
objects that have been put in front of me by a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:39.920 --> 00:29:50.600
guest who I admire and aspire to be more like.
Oftentimes it's not a question of figuring out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:50.600 --> 00:29:59.040
what to add. It's rather a question of looking&nbsp;
very closely at why you are failing to implement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:59.040 --> 00:30:05.160
the few things that you know reliably work and&nbsp;
then removing those impediments. All right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:05.160 --> 00:30:09.080
you have resistance. There are certain&nbsp;
obstacles or things that are preventing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:09.080 --> 00:30:14.760
you from reengaging with these things. You're&nbsp;
doing them consistently. What are those? How&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:14.760 --> 00:30:23.080
can you make them automatic? How can you look at&nbsp;
the work of say, BJ Fogg and perhaps James Clear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:23.080 --> 00:30:30.280
Atomic Habits, so that you can build these things&nbsp;
into automatic behaviors like brushing your teeth?&nbsp;

00:30:30.280 --> 00:30:38.880
And those are phases that alternate for me.&nbsp;
Right now I'd say I am not in the new habit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:38.880 --> 00:30:44.640
accumulation phase, but rather looking back over&nbsp;
my experience over the last five to 10 years, what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:44.640 --> 00:30:51.280
are the things that consistently work, that work&nbsp;
almost every time I implement them consistently?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:51.280 --> 00:30:55.760
And how can I return to those things?
