00:48:44.920 --> 00:48:50.880
And you have this experience, which is tremendous.
And I actually first met, I think it's Gen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:50.880 --> 00:48:56.680
or Yamamoto anyway, at Brushstroke, I think&nbsp;
was the name of the restaurant in New York&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:56.680 --> 00:49:02.680
City where I bumped into him. At the time, I was&nbsp;
doing the food marathon from The 4-Hour Chef,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:02.680 --> 00:49:09.720
for those people who remember that, where I&nbsp;
had whatever it was, 26.2 dishes in 24 hours&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:09.720 --> 00:49:15.440
walking around New York City. And he was sitting&nbsp;
there with this ice pick and a number of tools,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:15.440 --> 00:49:21.640
chiseling huge blocks of ice into perfect&nbsp;
spheres to make his cocktails, and we struck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:21.640 --> 00:49:27.360
up a conversation. When a friend of mine invited&nbsp;
me to this place in Tokyo, I was sitting there and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:27.360 --> 00:49:31.360
after the first or second drink, we both looked&nbsp;
at each other at the same time and we're like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:31.360 --> 00:49:37.000
"I know you." "I know you. Where do I know you&nbsp;
from?" And we put it together. There's that.&nbsp;

00:49:37.000 --> 00:49:44.360
I would say there is a semi underground whisky&nbsp;
bar that is quite well known in Niseko, up in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:44.360 --> 00:49:49.400
the North. If you go skiing, I would certainly&nbsp;
take a minute and check that out. There can't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:49.400 --> 00:49:55.520
be too many of them. And it's a husband and wife&nbsp;
team. The husband is Japanese and the wife is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:56.080 --> 00:50:02.280
I want to say Australian or British. I apologize&nbsp;
to her that I'm probably not getting it right.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:02.280 --> 00:50:09.200
It should be pretty easy to spot. And then,&nbsp;
if you can get to Nikko, N-I-K-K-O, in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

